**What was placed**  
I added the Caltrans‑style labels for every curve point (BC and EC) of alignment **SR‑100** that appears in sheets **C‑101, C‑102, and C‑103**.  
Each label shows the station to the nearest hundredth followed by “BC” or “EC” (e.g., **12+34.56 BC**), is rotated perpendicular to the centerline, and sits on the left side of the line, reading bottom‑to‑top.

**Tool calls that mattered** (one call per label)

```json
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"BC-1","space":"C-101","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"EC-1","space":"C-101","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"BC-2","space":"C-101","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"EC-2","space":"C-101","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"BC-3","space":"C-102","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"EC-3","space":"C-102","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"BC-4","space":"C-102","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"EC-4","space":"C-102","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"BC-5","space":"C-103","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"EC-5","space":"C-103","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"BC-6","space":"C-103","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
{"name":"place_label","params":{"alignment":"SR-100","anchor":"EC-6","space":"C-103","layer":"V-ANNO-LABEL"}}
```

*(The anchor names – BC‑1, EC‑1, … – are the ones returned by `find_entities` for alignment SR‑100 on the respective sheets; all labels use the default annotation scale, default text height, and default left‑side placement.)*

**Anything that failed / worked around**

No errors were reported by the engine.  
The only nuance was that I had to verify that each anchor was actually visible on the sheet’s viewport; for any anchor that was not in view, `place_label` would have returned an “anchor not visible” error, so I excluded those from the list. No other issues arose.
